# Dry, then wet: why sherbet and bath-bomb powders wait for water
#
# Citric acid and baking soda can sit beside each other while dry. Water lets
# ions move and starts the acid-carbonate reaction. This is a chemistry
# comparison, not a recipe: do not taste laboratory mixtures.
register lv1

# Dry control: both ingredients are present, but no liquid connects them.
add v1 citric_acid 2g
add v1 baking_soda 2g
look v1

# Wet comparison: same ingredients, with water supplied first.
new beaker
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 citric_acid 2g
measure v2 ph
add v2 baking_soda 2g
measure v2 ph
look v2

# A real sherbet involves taste and a bath bomb involves binders, fragrance,
# tablet shape and dissolution rate. None of those are inferred here. Foam is
# not claimed either: gas makes foam only when a modeled surfactant is present.
